# The #504 witness matrix (generated; the cross-cog column is in
# cogs.rs, the refusals in diagnostics.rs): target x conformance path
# x witness source x module arguments, each cell printing what runs
# through `Type[M]`, `T <: M` and a direct call where the extension is
# active. The expected output was computed from the rules, not taken
# from a run: the witness is the extension's own `def self.`, else the
# first of the signature in the target's class-side order with the
# extension active (its own class methods, its own includes, the
# extension's includes with what they bring, then a superclass's), the
# included module's own default where the walk reaches it (#669's
# decision (y): so the module's default comes before a superclass's
# method, the `ext/sup` cells); it runs for the target and its subclasses
# alike, unless a subclass conforms on its own (its own extension's
# witness); an own include goes by ordinary dispatch.
# Skipped as identical by the rules or not expressible:
# - module target (an extension of a module including one with class methods): refused, #530 (diagnostics.rs)
# - own/super_own paths x witness ext/nmod: an extension including the module the class has by an own include is refused (diagnostics test); N brought by an own include is ordinary dispatch, as `own`
# - own/super_own paths x witness sup: ordinary dispatch of a superclass's class method, the same as `own` one class up
# - own/super_own paths x module target: a module includes no class to run
# - mod_ext paths: they need the module target
# - witness sup x module target: a module has no superclass
# - args param x non-generic targets: no class parameter to pass
# - generic target x args concrete x witness sup: `B[U].d(x: U)` is no witness of `M[Int].d(x: Int)` (another signature), refused as an override in its own diagnostics, not a run cell
# - abstract target x path own/super_own: same as class
# - module target x args param: `Mid` has no parameter of its own
module M0
  def self.d -> String = "M"
end
class X0
  include M0
  def initialize; end
  def self.d -> String = "own"
end
def f0(t: Type[M0]) -> String = t.d
def g0[T <: M0](t: Type[T]) -> String = t.d
puts "class/own/own/none: #{f0(X0)} #{g0(X0)} #{X0.d}"
module M1[T]
  def self.d(x: T) -> String = "M"
end
class X1
  include M1[Int]
  def initialize; end
  def self.d(x: Int) -> String = "own"
end
def f1(t: Type[M1[Int]]) -> String = t.d(1)
def g1[T <: M1[Int]](t: Type[T]) -> String = t.d(1)
puts "class/own/own/concrete: #{f1(X1)} #{g1(X1)} #{X1.d(1)}"
